## Custom Build Example

To build the sample custom version:

1. Clean your build directory of any previous build.
2. Rename the directory from `custom-example` to `custom`.
3. Change to the `custom` directory.
4. Build QGC.

![Custom Build Screenshot](README.jpg)

For more information, see the [QGC Dev Guide](https://dev.qgroundcontrol.com/en/custom_build/custom_build.html).

### Main Features of the Example

- Assumes an "off the shelf" commercial vehicle; most setup options are hidden, as they are preconfigured by the manufacturer.
- The UI is simplified by hiding unnecessary elements for the target user.
- Advanced features remain accessible in "Advanced Mode."
- Custom branding is applied (images, color palette) to match corporate identity.
- Portions of the interface are customized (e.g., a custom instrument widget replaces the standard UI).
- Application settings are overridden to hide or adjust defaults as needed.
- The source code is fully commented to explain the rationale for each customization.
